# analog-smoke

Wire the PWM output named in main.cpp through a 10 kOhm resistor to the ADC
pin, and place a 1 uF capacitor from the ADC pin to ground: on a Pico or
Pico 2 that is GP16 through 10 kOhm to GP26, and 1 uF from GP26 to ground.
GP17, the other comparator of GP16's slice, and GP0, the alias of GP16's
comparator, stay unconnected; they are claimed and released only to prove the
sibling and alias rules. The check drives a one-kilohertz waveform at a
quarter, a half, and three quarters duty and reads the filtered level as a raw
count, so it needs no calibrated reference and asserts no temperature.

The application skips only when the first configure of either facility
answers Unsupported; a supported facility with an unwired fixture fails. It
releases what it claimed on every exit path. The firmware image build cannot
prove the analog path; run it with the fixture and a USB CDC console to see
the verdict.

Exit codes:

| Code | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| 0 | All checks passed, or a facility was unavailable and skipped. |
| 1–3 | ADC or PWM configure, or the period read, failed. |
| 4–6 | Sibling at another period, sibling at the same period, or alias rule failed. |
| 7–8 | GPIO ownership of the PWM or ADC pin was not refused. |
| 9 | A duty past the period was accepted, or a refused call changed its output. |
| 10 | A raw count fell outside the channel's range. |
| 11–13 | Quarter, half, or three-quarter duty read outside a tenth of full scale; inspect the fixture. |
| 14 | The temperature channel could not be read. |
| 15–16 | Release failed, or the pins did not return to GPIO afterwards. |
